IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mrca-member`
IMPORT `mrca-guide`

-- Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- the dollar amounts, from the formulas
-- the text deposit lost. Beside mrca-member.l4 (which answers which incapacity rate applies, and which lump-sum shares
-- are open) and mrca-guide.l4 (the Guide's weekly permanent impairment amount); this module gives the s 78(5) lump sum,
-- the former member's weekly incapacity compensation in dollars (ss 129 to 131), normal earnings for a former Permanent
-- Forces member (ss 141, 179), and the s 404 indexation factor.
--
-- SEAT: the current or former member, as in mrca-member.l4.
--
-- FORMULAS. Taken from ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A01285.formulas.md (transcribed 2026-10-24 from the authorised
-- Word rendering of the same compilation, each checked against the equation image). Each rule quotes its formula in that
-- file's linear notation.
--
-- FIGURES THAT ARE INPUTS. The Australian Government Actuary's conversion advice (s 78(5), (6)), the CPI December index
-- numbers (s 404), the $100 of s 141(1) as indexed under s 183, the national minimum wage (s 179), and the person's ADF
-- pay, allowances and actual earnings. The normal earnings of Reservists, cadets and declared members (Divisions 4 to 9
-- of Part 4 of Chapter 4) are an input to the weekly question; only Division 3 (Permanent Forces) is computed here.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as
-- advice. See NOTES.md (findings 15 to 20).

§ `Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004 -- the amounts, from the formulas`

§§ `s 78(5), (6) -- the lump sum` -- arises only if the person has chosen to convert weekly permanent impairment compensation

-- s 78(5): "The amount of the lump sum is worked out using the following formula:
--     Weekly amount converted to a lump sum − Appropriate percentage of the weekly amounts paid to the person on or after
--     the notice date and before the Commission became aware of the choice
-- where: appropriate percentage means the percentage chosen by the person under subsection (1). notice date means the
-- date specified in the notice given to the person under section 76. weekly amount converted to a lump sum means the
-- appropriate percentage of the weekly amount payable to the person, as at the date of the notice ..., converted to a lump
-- sum in accordance with advice from the Australian Government Actuary by reference to the person's age at that date."
-- (6): "a lump sum that can be payable to a person must not exceed that worked out by reference to the conversion to a
-- lump sum of a periodic payment payable to a male aged 30." The Actuary's advice is not deposited: it is asked as a
-- conversion factor (the lump sum per dollar of weekly amount) for the person's age, and for a male aged 30; (6) is read
-- as capping the converted amount, before the deduction (an INFERENCE). A percentage that s 78(1) does not open to the
-- person (mrca-member.l4's `What share may I convert to a lump sum`) gives NOTHING.
GIVEN `the weekly amount in the notice` IS A NUMBER
      `the s 74 maximum weekly amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the appropriate percentage` IS A NUMBER
      `the Actuary's conversion factor for my age` IS A NUMBER
      `the Actuary's conversion factor for a male aged 30` IS A NUMBER
      `the weekly amounts paid since the notice date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the s 78(5) lump sum` MEANS
    IF elem `the appropriate percentage` (`What share may I convert to a lump sum` `the weekly amount in the notice` `the s 74 maximum weekly amount`)
    THEN JUST (`the converted amount` MINUS (`the share` TIMES `the weekly amounts paid since the notice date`))
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the share` MEANS `the appropriate percentage` DIVIDED BY 100
        `the converted amount` MEANS
            `the share` TIMES `the weekly amount in the notice`
            TIMES (min `the Actuary's conversion factor for my age` `the Actuary's conversion factor for a male aged 30`)

@export How much is my permanent impairment lump sum, on the weekly amount in my notice (s 78(5), (6))?
GIVEN `my weekly amount in the notice` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly amount of permanent impairment compensation in the Commission's s 76 notice, in dollars
      `the maximum weekly amount in force` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 74 maximum weekly amount in force, in dollars ($233.07 in the Act, indexed each 1 July under s 404)
      `the percentage I chose to convert` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage of the weekly amount you chose to convert: 25, 50, 75 or 100
      `the conversion factor for my age` IS A NUMBER @desc The Australian Government Actuary's factor for converting a weekly amount to a lump sum at your age on the notice date (the lump sum for each dollar a week)
      `the conversion factor for a male aged 30` IS A NUMBER @desc The Actuary's factor for a male aged 30 (the s 78(6) cap)
      `the weekly amounts paid to me since the notice date` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of the weekly amounts paid to you on or after the notice date and before the Commission became aware of your choice, in dollars
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much is my lump sum` MEANS
    `the s 78(5) lump sum` `my weekly amount in the notice` `the maximum weekly amount in force` `the percentage I chose to convert` `the conversion factor for my age` `the conversion factor for a male aged 30` `the weekly amounts paid to me since the notice date`

@export How much is my permanent impairment lump sum, on the Guide's weekly amount (s 78(5), (6), Guide Chapter 23)?
GIVEN `the kind of my service` IS A `Kind of service` @desc The kind of service the conditions relate to (warlike or non-warlike: Table 23.1; any other: Table 23.2)
      `my impairment points` IS A NUMBER @desc Your combined impairment rating under the Guide
      `my lifestyle rating` IS A NUMBER @desc Your lifestyle rating, 0 to 7
      `the s 74 maximum in force` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 74 maximum weekly amount in force, in dollars ($233.07 in the Act, indexed each 1 July under s 404)
      `the percentage I chose` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage of the weekly amount you chose to convert: 25, 50, 75 or 100
      `the Actuary's factor for my age` IS A NUMBER @desc The Australian Government Actuary's factor for converting a weekly amount to a lump sum at your age on the notice date
      `the Actuary's factor for a male aged 30` IS A NUMBER @desc The Actuary's factor for a male aged 30 (the s 78(6) cap)
      `the weekly amounts I was paid since the notice date` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of the weekly amounts paid to you on or after the notice date and before the Commission became aware of your choice, in dollars
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much is my lump sum on the Guide's amount` MEANS
    CONSIDER `What weekly amount does the Guide give me` `the kind of my service` `my impairment points` `my lifestyle rating` `the s 74 maximum in force`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST w THEN `the s 78(5) lump sum` w `the s 74 maximum in force` `the percentage I chose` `the Actuary's factor for my age` `the Actuary's factor for a male aged 30` `the weekly amounts I was paid since the notice date`

§§ `ss 132, 141, 179 -- normal and actual earnings`

-- s 132(1): "actual earnings for a person for a week means the greater of the following amounts: (a) the weekly amount
-- (if any) that the person is able to earn in suitable work; (b) the amount (if any) that the person earns for the week
-- (including from allowances other than expense allowances) from any work that is undertaken by the person during the
-- week." Bonuses are left out (s 180(2)).
GIVEN `able to earn in suitable work` IS A NUMBER
      `earned this week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`actual earnings` MEANS max `able to earn in suitable work` `earned this week`

-- s 141(1): for a person who was a Permanent Forces member immediately before last ceasing to be a member, "the amount
-- worked out using the following formula:
--     Person's ADF pay for the week + Person's allowance component for the week + $100"
-- (the $100 is indexed under s 183). (2): ADF pay is what the person "would have earned for the week as a Permanent Forces
-- member if ... still a Permanent Forces member; and ... not incapacitated for service"; (3): the allowance component is
-- the compensable pay-related allowances that would then have been paid. s 179: if normal earnings are "less than an amount
-- calculated by multiplying the relevant minimum wage set by a national minimum wage order ... by 38 hours per week", they
-- are that amount instead. Bonuses and expected increases are left out (s 180(1)). Out: the Part 5 adjustments.
@export As a former Permanent Forces member, what are my normal earnings for a week (ss 141, 179)?
GIVEN `my ADF pay for the week` IS A NUMBER @desc The pay you would have earned this week as a Permanent Forces member if you were still serving and not incapacitated, in dollars (no bonuses)
      `my allowance component for the week` IS A NUMBER @desc The compensable pay-related allowances you would have been paid this week if still serving and not incapacitated (those paid to you just before you left), in dollars
      `the s 141 $100 in force` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 141(1) amount in force, in dollars ($100 in the Act, indexed under s 183)
      `the national minimum wage per hour` IS A NUMBER @desc The relevant minimum wage per hour set by the national minimum wage order under s 294 of the Fair Work Act 2009, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my normal earnings as a former Permanent Forces member` MEANS
    max (`my ADF pay for the week` PLUS `my allowance component for the week` PLUS `the s 141 $100 in force`)
        (`the national minimum wage per hour` TIMES 38)

§§ `ss 129 to 131 -- weekly incapacity compensation in dollars` -- arises only if a former member cannot work, or work as before

-- s 129(1): for a maximum rate week, "Person's normal earnings for the week − Person's actual earnings for the week".
-- s 131(1): for any later week, "(Person's adjustment percentage for the week × Person's normal earnings for the week) −
-- Person's actual earnings for the week". s 130(1): if during a week the s 129(2)(b) total "exceeds 45 times the normal
-- weekly hours", (2) pays the maximum rate hours at "(Person's maximum rate hours / Person's normal weekly hours) ×
-- (Person's normal earnings for the week − Person's actual earnings for the week)", and (3) the reduced rate hours at
-- "(Person's reduced rate hours / Person's normal weekly hours) × Person's reduced compensation amount", with reduced rate
-- hours "Person's normal weekly hours − Person's maximum rate hours" and the reduced compensation amount "the amount of
-- compensation worked out in accordance with section 131 if that section had applied for the whole week". Maximum rate
-- hours are "the total number of hours in the week ... that would have counted towards the person's normal weekly hours
-- ... and ... that elapse before the total ... exceeds 45 times the person's normal weekly hours"; the encoding takes the
-- hours this week's incapacity prevents as spread evenly over the week's normal hours, so maximum rate hours = NWH × (the
-- hours left ÷ the hours lost this week); in a week of total incapacity, the hours left (an INFERENCE where the incapacity
-- is partial). Unlike the Comcare Act, the MRCA has no AWOTE cap and no minimum earnings top-up here (s 179 raises normal
-- earnings instead). A negative result is read as nil (an INFERENCE). Out: Subdivisions B and D (hospital patients,
-- superannuation), s 138 (small amounts converted).
@export As a former ADF member unable to work, how much incapacity compensation do I get this week, in dollars (ss 118 to 122, 129 to 131)?
GIVEN `I am a former member kept from work by an accepted condition this week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have left the ADF and an accepted service injury or disease stops you working your normal weekly hours, or at your former level, this week (and you have claimed)
      `I have chosen the Special Rate Disability Pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have chosen to receive the Special Rate Disability Pension under Part 6
      `my normal weekly hours of work` IS A NUMBER @desc Your normal weekly hours as s 132 works them out (37.5 for a former Permanent Forces member)
      `the hours lost to incapacity before this week` IS A NUMBER @desc The total hours, in all earlier maximum rate weeks, that the incapacity has stopped you working (or working at your former level)
      `the hours lost to incapacity this week` IS A NUMBER @desc The hours of your normal weekly hours that the incapacity stops you working (or working at your former level) this week
      `the hours I work this week` IS A NUMBER @desc The hours you work this week (0 if none)
      `I have reached pension age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have reached pension age under the Social Security Act 1991
      `my condition began within 2 years before pension age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you sustained the injury or contracted the disease at or after the age 2 years before your pension age
      `the weeks of incapacity compensated so far` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of incapacity have already been compensated (counted only for a condition within 2 years before pension age)
      `I am in prison for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are in prison this week in connection with your conviction of an offence
      `my normal earnings for the week` IS A NUMBER @desc Your normal earnings for the week under s 132(2), in dollars (for a former Permanent Forces member, the question above works them out)
      `the weekly amount I am able to earn in suitable work` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly amount the Commission determines you are able to earn in suitable work, in dollars (0 if none)
      `what I earn this week from work` IS A NUMBER @desc What you earn this week from any work, including allowances other than expense allowances, in dollars (no bonuses; 0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much incapacity compensation this week` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Which incapacity rate applies` `I am a former member kept from work by an accepted condition this week` `I have chosen the Special Rate Disability Pension` `my normal weekly hours of work` `the hours lost to the end of this week` `the hours I work this week` `I have reached pension age` `my condition began within 2 years before pension age` `the weeks of incapacity compensated so far` `I am in prison for an offence`
    WHEN `a maximum rate week: compensation on my full normal earnings less my actual earnings (s 129)` THEN JUST `the s 129 amount`
    WHEN `a reduced rate week: compensation on this adjustment percentage of my normal earnings less my actual earnings (s 131)` `adj` THEN
        IF `the hours lost to incapacity before this week` LESS THAN `the 45-week total`
        THEN JUST (((`the maximum rate hours` DIVIDED BY `my normal weekly hours of work`) TIMES `the s 129 amount`)
                   PLUS (((`my normal weekly hours of work` MINUS `the maximum rate hours`) DIVIDED BY `my normal weekly hours of work`) TIMES (`the s 131 amount` `adj`)))
        ELSE JUST (`the s 131 amount` `adj`)
    WHEN `the Special Rate Disability Pension I chose, worked out under Part 6 (s 118(2)(a)), which is not encoded` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST 0
    WHERE
        `the hours lost to the end of this week` MEANS `the hours lost to incapacity before this week` PLUS `the hours lost to incapacity this week`
        `the 45-week total` MEANS 45 TIMES `my normal weekly hours of work`
        `my actual earnings` MEANS `actual earnings` `the weekly amount I am able to earn in suitable work` `what I earn this week from work`
        `the s 129 amount` MEANS max 0 (`my normal earnings for the week` MINUS `my actual earnings`)
        `the maximum rate hours` MEANS
            `my normal weekly hours of work`
            TIMES ((`the 45-week total` MINUS `the hours lost to incapacity before this week`) DIVIDED BY `the hours lost to incapacity this week`)
        `the s 131 amount` MEANS
            GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER
            YIELD max 0 ((`a` DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES `my normal earnings for the week`) MINUS `my actual earnings`)

§§ `s 404 -- indexation of amounts`

-- s 404(2): "The dollar amount mentioned in the provision, for an indexation year in which the indexation factor is
-- greater than 1, is replaced by the amount worked out using the formula:
--     Dollar amount for the provision for the previous financial year × Indexation factor for the indexation year"
-- (3): "The indexation factor for an indexation year is the number worked out using the following formula:
--     December index number for the previous financial year / Highest December index number for a year before the
--     previous financial year"
-- (4): "calculated to 3 decimal places, but increased by .001 if the fourth decimal place is more than 4" (read as
-- truncation then the increase, an INFERENCE). (5A): for the s 74(1) amount, "the indexation factor is reduced by the
-- brought-forward CPI indexation amount for the year, but not below 1" -- 0.007 less any earlier reductions (6), an input.
-- (5B): the year of the denominator "must be no earlier than 2024". The December index number is the All Groups CPI,
-- weighted average of the 8 capital cities (6). s 404(1) lists the amounts: ss 74(1), 80(2), 82(3), 138(1)(a), 206(3),
-- 216(1)(b), 219(1)(b), 234(2), 240(3), 252, 254, 263(1)(a), (b), 267(3)(a).
GIVEN `the December index number for the previous financial year` IS A NUMBER
      `the highest earlier December index number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 404 indexation factor to 3 places` MEANS
    IF `fourth place` GREATER THAN 4 THEN `three places` PLUS 0.001 ELSE `three places`
    WHERE
        `ratio`        MEANS `the December index number for the previous financial year` DIVIDED BY `the highest earlier December index number`
        `three places` MEANS FLOOR (`ratio` TIMES 1000) DIVIDED BY 1000
        `fourth place` MEANS FLOOR (`ratio` TIMES 10000) MINUS (FLOOR (`ratio` TIMES 1000) TIMES 10)

@export What does an MRCA dollar amount become for an indexation year (s 404)?
GIVEN `the dollar amount for the previous financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount for the provision for the previous financial year, in dollars (the Act's figure, or the last replacement)
      `the December CPI for the previous financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc The All Groups CPI (weighted average of the 8 capital cities) for the December quarter in the previous financial year
      `the highest December CPI for an earlier year, from 2024` IS A NUMBER @desc The highest December quarter CPI number for a year before that one, counting no year earlier than 2024 (s 404(5B))
      `it is the s 74(1) maximum weekly amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the amount is the s 74(1) maximum weekly amount of permanent impairment compensation
      `the brought-forward CPI indexation amount left` IS A NUMBER @desc For the s 74(1) amount: what is left of the 0.007 brought-forward CPI indexation amount after earlier years' reductions (s 404(6); 0 once used up)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the MRCA amount for the indexation year` MEANS
    IF `the factor` GREATER THAN 1
    THEN `the dollar amount for the previous financial year` TIMES `the factor`
    ELSE `the dollar amount for the previous financial year`
    WHERE
        `the raw factor` MEANS `the s 404 indexation factor to 3 places` `the December CPI for the previous financial year` `the highest December CPI for an earlier year, from 2024`
        `the factor` MEANS
            IF `it is the s 74(1) maximum weekly amount`
            THEN max 1 (`the raw factor` MINUS `the brought-forward CPI indexation amount left`)
            ELSE `the raw factor`
